vie was shot under the name  fall of George so they're sticking with  their classic tradition by having the  running title for spider-man 3 be  serenity now now there's a lot that's  been happening recently with the  development of spider-man 3 everything  is in pre-production right now but there  have been a lot of meetings with the  studio and Tom  Hollan about the film so things are very  well underway in fact Tom Holland has  recently revealed that he is met with  Marvel Studios and talked to Sony of  course about the film and about their  future plans for spider-man in the MCU  and he said that he met with Marvel and  Sony and now he knows everything  so Tom Holland has officially been told  everything that is going on with  spider-man and everything that is going  to happen with him in the future so  hopefully he pulls a classic Tom and  spills the beans soon but Kevin Feige  has also recently opened up about what  to expect in the next spider-man film of  the franchise now in the past after the  spider-man Disney Sony deal came to a  completion Kevin Feige opened up and  told us a little bit about what to  expect and he said far from home sets up  a Peter Parker story that has never been  done before on film and he implied that  this film is not only going to be  different than anything we've seen  before but also bigger and recently he  opened up again about what we can expect  he said Spidey will be in his element  out of the shadow of Tony and the  Avengers as his own man and hero now so  in spider-man 3 we're really going to  see Peter Parker shine as his own person  and spider-man homecoming he was  definitely under the wing of Tony Stark  and the same goes for infinity war and  Avengers end game and then again in  spider-man far from home Tony's presence  was definitely felt all throughout the  movie and then of course he had Mysterio  who he thought was going to be a mentor  for him but of course we know how that  turned out and then he had happy happy  was there to take care of him he was  there with the jet to make his new  spider-man suit he was there with the  pep talk  happy gave him the motivation that he  needed to go and defeat Mysterio but now  according to Kevin Feige he's not going  to have any of that in the next film and  if we think about how spider-man far  from home left off in the post-credits  scene it makes a lot of sense Peter  Parker's identity is revealed everybody  knows that he is spider-man and  everybody thinks that he's a murderer  everyone thinks he killed Mysterio so  he's going to be on the run and he  probably won't be able to contact most  of the people that he knows and loves so  it seems like this next film is really  going to be about just spider-man just  Peter Parker all about him and how we  can step up on his own and become a hero  and this is coming to  directly from Kevin Feige so we can't  expect this but what can we expect as  far as the villain is concerned well of  course we know about Kraven the hunter  and the possibility of the sinister six  however recently we've heard a rumor  about Norman Osborn  now before spider-man far from home came  out there were some people that said  they saw a pre-screening of far from  home and in the post-credits scene they  showed Norman Osborn in this post-credit  scene we saw Norman Osborn assembling  the sinister six now this was not of  course in the final cut of the movie but  some people who saw it like Grace  Randolph claimed that this is indeed  what they did see and now it appears  that we have somebody on reddit who says  that they know what happened and what is  going to happen with Norman Osborn so of  course this was posted anonymously and  it says so before I tell you about what  Marvel's current plan for Osborn is let  me tell you what their plan was so  before spider-man fire from home  released Marvel had a huge plan for  Norman Osborn in the MCU with him being  one of the main antagonists in fact in  the original script there was a  post-credits scene that featured him  however in the months leading up to the  film's release talks between Marvel and  Sony turned bitter and they decided to  put their plans for Osborn on the  backburner because they could lose his  rights at any second now this very well  could have happened we don't really know  the ins and outs of what really happened  between Sony and Disney we have our  speculation and we've heard rumors but  we don't know 100% but it does make  sense that if Marvel and Disney didn't  know if they were going to have  spider-man in the MCU in the future they  wouldn't want to introduce Norman Osborn  because then nothing would happen and  we'd have a dead end with that story  so if plans really did fall through  right before spider-man far from home  got released and they were planning to  introduce Norman Osborn it would make  sense that Marvel and Disney decided to  delay their introduction of Norman  Osborn but they go on to say now that  Marvel and Sony have a new deal however  Marvel has a new plan for Osborn the  current plan is to make him a shadow  villain much like Palpatine from Star  Wars or Voldemort from Harry Potter and  they plan to make him this in spider-man  3 so this is kind of going to be like  ant-man and the wasp we heard there is a  benefactor but we never learned who it  was  and it could be Osborne if that's  Marvel's plans but this will set up  Norman Osborn for a much bigger role in  the MCU Osborn like spider-man and Jay  jonah Jameson will also have some  appearances in Sony's Marvel Universe  and will be a part of the connective  glue that unites the two film universes  however Sony themselves don't have big  plans for the character and he'll mainly  be a part of the mainline MCU Marvel  does have plans for the Dark Avengers  but not until at least much later in  phase 5 and for those of you who are not  aware Norman Osborn and the comics is  the leader of the Dark Avengers now this  of course is 